Single-database configuration for Flask.

Alembic migrations contain schema changes only. Update task content and other
application data directly in the database, independently of schema upgrades.

The data-only migration tail was removed on 2026-09-16. The final schema
migration (adding tasks.gpt_rate_limit) keeps the deployed head f3a5c7e9b1d4,
so a database already at that revision needs no migration or restamping.
Fresh databases receive the same schema without requiring existing task rows.
Databases at an intermediate revision from the removed history must have their
schema checked and revision reconciled before upgrading with this history.
